<div class="container py-5">
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
      <div class="card shadow-sm">
        <div class="card-body p-5">
          <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-4">Event Attending Policy</h1>

          <p class="lead mb-4">Last Updated: <%= toISTDateString(new Date()) %></p>

          <div class="mb-4">
            <p>This Event Attending Policy sets forth the rules and conditions applicable to attendees of events and concerts accessed or purchased through the Rapira platform ("Platform"). By attending any event, you agree to comply with this Policy along with the Terms of Service, Refund Policy, and any rules imposed by the event organizer or venue.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">1. Admission Requirements</h2>
            <p>Entry to an event may require:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>a valid ticket</li>
              <li>government-issued photo ID</li>
              <li>age verification where applicable</li>
              <li>compliance with venue security checks</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Entry may be refused if:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>the ticket is invalid, altered, duplicated, or reported stolen</li>
              <li>you do not meet age or identification requirements</li>
              <li>you violate venue rules or this policy</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The organizer or venue reserves the right to deny admission without refund in case of policy violations.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">2. Minimum Age Requirement</h2>
            <p>Unless otherwise stated by the organizer:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>the Platform is intended for users 15 years of age or older</li>
              <li>some events may carry higher age limits (e.g., 18+)</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Parents/guardians are responsible for minors permitted to attend.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">3. Ticket Validity</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>each ticket admits one person only</li>
              <li>tickets purchased from unauthorized resellers are invalid</li>
              <li>damaged, altered, or tampered tickets may be rejected</li>
              <li>Lost tickets may not be replaced.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">4. Ticket Validation & Entry Control (Mandatory)</h2>
            <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold mt-3">4.1 Ticket must be scanned at entry</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>All attendees must present their ticket at the entrance for verification and scanning by authorized security personnel.</li>
              <li>entry is permitted only after the ticket is successfully scanned and validated</li>
              <li>merely possessing a ticket does not guarantee entry</li>
              <li>attendees must comply with scanning and security instructions</li>
            </ul>
            <p>If a ticket cannot be validated, entry may be refused.</p>
            <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold mt-3">4.2 Entering without scanning is prohibited</h3>
            <p>Attempting to:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>enter without scanning</li>
              <li>bypass security</li>
              <li>sneak into the venue</li>
            </ul>
            <p>is strictly prohibited.</p>
            <p>If someone is found inside the venue without a validated ticket, they may:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>be removed from the venue</li>
              <li>be charged a penalty or fine as per organizer/venue rules</li>
              <li>be reported to authorities where applicable</li>
              <li>be banned from future events</li>
            </ul>
            <p>No refund will be issued in such cases.</p>
            <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold mt-3">4.3 Single use only — no re-scanning</h3>
            <p>Each ticket is valid for single entry only, unless explicitly stated otherwise by the organizer.</p>
            <p>The following actions are prohibited:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>scanning the same ticket again after entry</li>
              <li>attempting re-entry with already validated ticket</li>
              <li>sharing QR/barcode with others</li>
              <li>using screenshots or duplicate tickets</li>
            </ul>
            <p>If a validated ticket is scanned again:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>entry will be refused</li>
              <li>penalties or fines may apply according to venue rules or law</li>
              <li>the ticket may be permanently blocked without refund</li>
            </ul>
            <h3 class="h5 fw-semibold mt-3">4.4 Fraudulent ticket use</h3>
            <p>The following are treated as fraud:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>entering without validation</li>
              <li>duplicating tickets</li>
              <li>manipulating QR codes/barcodes</li>
              <li>using canceled/invalid tickets</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Fraud may result in:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>denial of entry</li>
              <li>cancellation of tickets</li>
              <li>account suspension</li>
              <li>legal action as per applicable law</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">5. Late Entry and Re-Entry</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>late entry is subject to organizer rules</li>
              <li>some events may prohibit entry after commencement</li>
              <li>re-entry is usually not allowed unless specifically permitted</li>
            </ul>
            <p>No refund is issued for late arrival.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">6. Conduct & Behavior</h2>
            <p>Attendees must:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>behave respectfully toward staff, artists, and others</li>
              <li>comply with venue and security instructions</li>
            </ul>
            <p>The following are prohibited:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>abusive, violent, or disruptive conduct</li>
              <li>harassment</li>
              <li>property damage</li>
              <li>entering restricted areas</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Violation may result in removal without refund.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">7. Prohibited Items</h2>
            <p>Unless otherwise allowed by the organizer, items such as:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>weapons or sharp objects</li>
              <li>illegal substances</li>
              <li>outside alcohol</li>
              <li>fireworks</li>
              <li>professional recording equipment</li>
              <li>large bags</li>
            </ul>
            <p>may be restricted or banned.</p>
            <p>Security checks may be conducted.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">8. Audio, Video & Photography</h2>
            <p>Unless expressly permitted:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>professional recording is prohibited</li>
              <li>flash photography may be restricted</li>
            </ul>
            <p>By attending, you consent to being photographed/filmed as part of event media.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">9. Weather & Outdoor Events</h2>
            <p>For outdoor events:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>shows may continue in light weather conditions</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Refund rules:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>canceled 3–4 hours before event due to weather → ticket amount only refunded</li>
              <li>weather disruption during event → no refund</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Platform, convenience, or processing fees remain non-refundable.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">10. Health & Safety</h2>
            <p>Attendees must comply with venue health and safety instructions.</p>
            <p>Anyone posing risk may be refused entry.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">11. Liability Disclaimer</h2>
            <p>Attendance is at your own risk. Rapira is not liable for:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>loss of personal belongings</li>
              <li>injury due to crowd behavior</li>
              <li>actions of organizers or venue operators</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-4">
            <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">12. Contact</h2>
            <p>For event-related concerns:</p>
            <p>📧 vijaymudaliyar224@gmail.com</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>